  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new file, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole_reach.rs`, holds `reach_up`, `upper_levels` and `band_sweep`. When a ring of a deeper band has a tool sweep that reaches outside every sweep cut so far, `reach_up` adds levels above the ring's first level (`upper_levels`). Each pass is then at most one stepdown under the pass before it on that ring.\n- `upper_levels` has three cases. The predicate is `stock_over`, the same predicate by which `cut_levels_under` keeps Top Z as a level.\n  - No stock over Top Z: the flat levels under Top Z. A level at Top Z removes no material and is not added.\n  - The stock top is less than one stepdown over Top Z: levels one stepdown at a time down from the stock top. These levels are off the flat grid on purpose. A pass at Top Z shares its plane with the band-0 ring there, and in `contour_whole_step` case 1 the lead of that ring crossed the grown ring (`Crossing`).\n  - The stock top is one stepdown or more over Top Z: Top Z and the flat levels under it. Band 0 bites the same depth at Top Z.\n- If the ring cannot be proven clear of the part at the added levels, the operation is refused by name. The toolpath is not made, so nothing posts.\n- A ring whose sweep stays inside the cut sweeps is not changed (an outline that does not grow).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs` keeps the union of the band sweeps (`cover`) and calls `reach_up` after `check_unread`.\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2597-new-outline-from-top-z.md`. The stepdown is the axial limit of the operation. So there is no new parameter: its other value would post the buried pass again. The entry also records the B1 fix and the dropped options.\n\n## Review fix B1 (second review)\n\n- Before: with the stock top over Top Z, `reach_up` added only the levels under Top Z. On the #2597 part with the stock top 28 (Top Z 25, stepdown 5), the base ring was first cut at Z 20, 8.000 mm under the stock top.\n- After: the base ring is cut at Z 23, 18, 13, 8, 5, 0 and the boss ring at Z 25, 20, 15, 10. With the stock top 31, the base ring takes Z 25, 20, 15, 10, 5, 0.\n- The first proposal (add the Top Z level always) gave `Crossing { moves: [3, 27] }` in `contour_whole_step` case 1 with the stock top 17. That is why the levels come from the stock top when it is less than one stepdown over Top Z.\n- Known limit: with the stock top one stepdown or more over Top Z, the two rings share the Top Z plane. On case 1 with the stock top 18.5 the verifier reports `Crossing` and blocks the post. This is visible and safe, but a correct part does not post. #2677 tracks it.\n- F3 (add to `cover` only the rings with levels after `trim_ladder`) is not done. A `Region` built from part of `band.loops` can split a hole from its outer ring. That is not a small change.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the fix, on the #2597 part (boss 30x30 to Z25 on a 60x60 base to Z10, D10, stepdown 5): the base ring was first cut at Z5, 20.000 mm under Top Z 25 (levels `[5.0, 0.0]`).\n- Before the fix, on a three-step part: the middle ring was first cut at Z18, 12.000 mm under Top Z 30.\n- After the fix: each ring steps down from Top Z (or from the stock top over it) in steps of at most the stepdown, and ends at its floor. The depth verifier gives no warning.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `contour_whole_new_outline` (5 passed):\n  - `new_larger_outline_below_top_z_steps_down_from_top_z`\n  - `every_new_outline_of_three_steps_steps_down_from_top_z`\n  - `new_outline_steps_down_from_a_stock_top_over_top_z` (B1 pin of the review; it fails at 0549b3fd1 with \"base ring: pass at Z 20 is 8.000 under Z 28\")\n  - `new_outline_takes_top_z_when_the_stock_stands_a_stepdown_over_it`\n  - `an_outline_that_does_not_grow_is_not_walked_again_above`\n- `camcraft-motion` `contour_whole`: `earlier_blind_hole_stop_does_not_hide_later_counterbore_change` has a changed pin. The upper bore now also has a lap at extent 7 at Z16 and Z12. This is correct: the stock core inside the upper bore grows there. All 8 tests pass.\n- `camcraft-app` `contour_whole_step`: all 3 tests pass. `case1_chamfered_island_top_contours_plate_to_bottom_with_tabs` now runs with the stock top at Top Z (dz 15) and over it (dz 17), each with the normal and the oversized stock. With dz 17 it asserts the pass at Z 13.5 of the grown island ring. No blocking warning in the four runs.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` at da40b954d: 122 steps, 0 failed, 24.6 min. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Parts with stock that is narrower than the part's outline. The added passes cut air there (see #2658).\n- Tabs on an added level of a new outline. The tab code was not changed.\n- The stock top one stepdown or more over Top Z with rings closer than the lead length (#2677).\n- A run in the GUI and a real post on a machine.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo CL or NC golden changed. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Shared files\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs` is also touched by #2538. This PR does not change `contour_depth.rs`.\n- This PR does not touch `tab_bridge.rs` or `contour.rs` (#2561).\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- #2658: start a new outline where the stock starts, not at Top Z.\n- #2677: a grown outline at Top Z can cross the band-0 ring when the stock top is one stepdown or more over Top Z.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Whole-model 2D Contour: a new, larger outline below Top Z is now cut from the top of the material (Top Z, or the stock top when it is over Top Z) down in steps no deeper than the stepdown, or the operation is refused by name. When the stock top is one stepdown or more over Top Z, the first pass is at Top Z, with the same bite as the rest of the operation. Before, its first pass buried the tool and posted with no warning.\n\nFixes #2597\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
